Binary Semaphore vs Mutex
Both can help ensure that only one thread accesses a shared resource at a time, but they work differently.


Feature
Binary Semaphore
Mutex
Values / state
0 or 1
Locked or unlocked


Main purpose
Signaling or synchronization; can also control exclusive access
Mutual exclusion



Ownership
No ownership requirement
Has an owner


Who can release it?
Generally, a different thread can signal it
Normally, the thread that locked it must unlock it



Example use
Notify another thread that data is ready
Protect a shared counter or data structure